  "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot ({e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
